# GDN chunk_delta_h: choose the launch tile from the grid, not from a single hardcoded config
#
# Base:   sglang git checkout at /sgl-workspace/sglang, commit
#         29481685462732237d80d86076d6563e1f658102 (SGLang 0.5.17)
#         The checkout has pre-existing unrelated dirty files from the image build
#         (python/pyproject.toml, python/sglang/kernels/aot/pyproject.toml, two deleted
#         pyproject_*.toml, untracked .hip sources). None is touched by this patch.
#
# Pristine copy of the edited file (the base to diff against, independent of git):
#         git show HEAD:python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/fla/chunk_delta_h.py \
#           > /tmp/chunk_delta_h.py.bak
#         verified byte-identical to the file before editing.
#
# Apply:  cd /sgl-workspace/sglang && git apply /path/to/patches/gdn_chunk_h_launch_config.patch
#         then restart the server -- this is python source read at import, no rebuild needed.
# Revert: cd /sgl-workspace/sglang && git apply -R /path/to/patches/gdn_chunk_h_launch_config.patch
#
# What it does
#   chunk_gated_delta_rule_fwd_kernel_h_blockdim64 launches on grid
#   (cdiv(V, BV), N * H). SGLang pins BV=32 through a *single-config* @triton.autotune --
#   deliberately, because the kernel writes the final recurrent state back into initial_state
#   in place, so a multi-config autotune benchmark phase would run many candidates over live
#   state and corrupt the pool. The consequence is that BV is fixed while the grid is not.
#   At this model's TP=4 shard (V=128, H=16) with chunked-prefill 16384 over ISL 8192, N is 1
#   or 2, so the grid is 64 or 128 workgroups on a 256-CU part: half to three quarters of the
#   device idle. This patch replaces the pinned config with an analytic rule that halves BV
#   when -- and only when -- the resulting grid still fits the device, and keeps 32/4/2
#   otherwise. The autotune key (H, K, V, BT, USE_GK, NT_BUCKET) could not have expressed this
#   even with more configs, because it does not contain N.
#
#   Output is unaffected: BV tiles V, which the kernel never reduces over.
#
# Kernel measurement (analysis/gdn/bench_chunk_h.py, torch.profiler device time,
# V=K=128 H=16 Hg=4 T=8192/seq, MI355X 256 CU):
#
#     N   shipped 32/4/2   this patch        speedup
#     1       369.45 us     272.78 (16/4/3)   1.354x
#     2       506.91 us     421.62 (16/4/3)   1.202x
#     3       540.21 us     481.05 (16/4/2)   1.123x
#     4       559.85 us     504.72 (16/4/2)   1.109x
#     8       719.04 us     718.71 (shipped)  1.000x
#
#   Production N is 1-2, so 1.20-1.35x on a kernel worth 7.70% of prefill device time, in a
#   benchmark that is 36% prefill: ~0.5% end-to-end on its own, which is BELOW this machine's
#   restart-to-restart floor (0.65-1.60%, FINDINGS.md section 1). It is therefore NOT claimed
#   as a standalone end-to-end delta. It was measured stacked -- see below.
#
# Correctness: analysis/gdn/check_chunk_h.py -- h, v_new and the in-place-updated recurrent
#   state are all bit-identical to the shipped tile on 8 shapes (N=1..4 at the production head
#   config, plus two other head configs and a K=V=64 case).
#
# End-to-end (frozen config, cold run discarded), stacked on the previously reported arm
# (patches/gemm_tuned_table_tp4.patch + patches/topk_softmax_ldg_width.patch) together with
# patches/fmoe_tuned_rows_tp4.patch:
#
#     arm                                          warm runs   tok/s     vs local baseline
#     baseline (frozen config)                       8 / 3      2505.96      --
#     + GEMM table + topk LDG width (reported arm)   8 / 2      2569.26      +2.53%
#     + this patch + fmoe_tuned_rows_tp4             8 / 2      2604.42      +3.93%
#
#   Increment over the reported arm: +1.37%. Run range [2597.63, 2611.06] against the reported
#   arm's [2565.87, 2574.29] -- disjoint. Against the 2490.308 tok/s in the task document,
#   +4.58%. mean TTFT 5001.6 -> 4979.2 ms, mean TPOT 20.04 -> 19.72 ms (both improve).
#   results/gdnmoe_w{1..4}_* (instance 1) and results/gdnmoeB_w{1..4}_* (instance 2);
#   gdnmoe_w0 / gdnmoeB_w0 were the cold runs and are discarded.
#   The two instances' warm means are 2605.87 and 2602.96 -- a 0.11% restart-to-restart spread,
#   smaller than either instance's own within-run spread, which is what makes +1.37% claimable.
#   Instance 2's discarded cold run was 2570.71, inside the reported arm's range: an undiscarded
#   first run would have erased this result entirely.
#   This patch's own share of that +1.37% is the ~0.5% estimated above; it is not separable
#   end to end and is not claimed separately.
#
#   Accuracy: gsm8k 5-shot strict-match 0.9727 +/- 0.0045 (1283/1319) for the stacked arm, gate
#   0.9691 -- passes. eval_results/gdnmoe_gsm8k_20260820_152553. Note that gate was run on the
#   stack; THIS patch cannot have contributed to the 6-answer drop from the 1289 baseline, because
#   its outputs are bit-identical to the shipped tile (analysis/gdn/check_chunk_h.py, 8 shapes,
#   torch.equal on h, v_new and the in-place recurrent state). The fp4 stage-1 intermediate in
#   patches/fmoe_tuned_rows_tp4.patch is the only numerics change in the arm.
#
# Stacking: applies cleanly on its own; it touches no file any other patch here touches.
#
# One difference between this patch and the exact build that was benchmarked, recorded for
# honesty: the server that produced the numbers above was started before the now-unused
# `autotune_cache_kwargs` import was dropped, so that build still carried the binding
# (`from ...fla.utils import (autotune_cache_kwargs, is_nvidia_hopper,)`) while this patch
# imports only `is_nvidia_hopper`. Removing @triton.autotune is what made the name unused. No
# behavioural difference: the same module is imported either way, the name was never referenced
# after the decorator was removed, and nothing in the kernel path reads it. Every other byte of
# the file is identical to the benchmarked build.
#
diff --git a/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/fla/chunk_delta_h.py b/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/fla/chunk_delta_h.py
